<header><p class="enc-kicker">Institution</p><h1 class="enc-title">Bhukti</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as bhuktis</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">A bhukti was a province in the administrative system of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gupta-empire">Gupta Empire</a>. Each bhukti was governed by an uparika, frequently a member of the royal family, and was divided into districts called <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vishaya">vishayas</a>. The system combined central oversight with the integration of local elites into government.</p></div>
